<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chikka Devaraja Wodeyar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1645">1645</a>–<a href="/years/1704">1704</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chikka <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devaraja">Devaraja</a> Wodeyar was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> from 1673 to 1704. He expanded the kingdom across southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, bought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengaluru">Bangalore</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in 1689 and organised the administration into eighteen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a>. He also reformed revenue collection and was a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chikka-devaraja-wodeyar.jpg" alt="Chikka Devaraja Wodeyar" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Artist unknown, photographer unknown, author: C. Hyavadana Rao · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chikkadevaraja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
